- `make relay-shell-test relay-shell-vet` — exit 0; all relay Go packages, 35 release-tool tests, and Go vet pass.
- `make relay-shell-build ...` — exit 0; all four pinned assets and canonical manifest emitted.
- `make relay-shell-verify` — exit 0.
- final native Darwin arm64 runtime gate — exit 0.
- 12-run native runtime stress loop — exit 0; 12/12 pass.
- `make relay-supply-chain-audit relay-toolchain-check` — exit 0.
- `actionlint -color` — exit 0, no diagnostics.
- Python `py_compile`, workflow YAML parse, shellcheck of existing relay smoke scripts, and `git diff --check` — exit 0.
- `task-board validate` — exit 1 on pre-existing/ancestor board state: `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` for `EPIC-260715-2lz67t` (`backlog` versus child aggregate `development`). A CLI-only repair attempt, `set_status(EPIC-260715-2lz67t, status=development)`, also exited 1 because the Epic is dependency-blocked by `EPIC-260715-2mqgvm` (`reviewing`) and `EPIC-260715-3810we` (`backlog`). No board file was edited directly and this unrelated ancestor dependency state is not reported as a passing gate.

